<title>USA: Norand stake cut by Gabelli group.</title>
<headline>Norand stake cut by Gabelli group.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by New York investment manager Mario Gabelli said Thursday it sold its stake in Norand Corp.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said its latest transactions include a net 395,200 common sold Feb 21 at $33.2449 to $33.50 per share.</p>
<p>As a result of the offer by Western Atlas Inc for all of Norand's common stock at $33.50 per share, the group ceased to own any stock, according to the filing.</p>
